# STIG AS24-U1-000180: The Apache web server log files must only be accessible by p
# STIG ID: V-214235 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `apache-as24-u1-000180-log-dir-perms-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `apache`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG AS24-U1-000180: The Apache web server log files must only be accessible by privileged users.`
    description `The Apache web server log files must only be accessible by privileged users.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `apache,stig,disa-stig,permissions`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:AS24-U1-000180,NIST-800-53:AU-9`
    control_objective `AU-9`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Apache:localhost:web-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA Apache STIG guidance for AS24-U1-000180.`

    component_id `comp-apache-web`

    impl_AU_9 `This control is validated by checking the Apache HTTP server configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        path `/var/log/httpd`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE meta_check
        exists boolean = true
        permissions string = `0750`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN file_metadata
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF meta_check
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
